{"reference":"2 Chronicles 10","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":10,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Division","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A debated way of reading the book’s perspective is that, after this division, the narrative follows the Davidic kings of Judah and the Jerusalem temple while still speaking of priests, Levites, worshipers, and captives from the northern tribes as part of “all Israel.”","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 10:1-19"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_010_73f3d60e3b35079864dc6aee"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}